# action</outer> creates position</q> itself, so when it publishes, the
# pending Guarantee of action</builder> on its own particle writes below a
# particle it created and stays pending. action</builder> creates
# position</q>::position</r>, whose Destructor fails its requirement on
# position</needed>, so destroying position<holder> must apply the Guarantees
# of action</outer> and report that failure.
define the potential action<my.domain.com:my_lib:/test> {
    it happens when {
        this particle is created.
    } and it does {
        define the position<holder> {
            it may only contain particles where {
                it has the action</wrapper>.
            }
        }
        create a particle in position<holder>.
        create a particle in position<holder>::action</wrapper>::position<run>.
    }
}
